<!-- What it is not -->
<section class="section tight" data-reveal>
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <p class="kicker">Clear on scope</p>
    <h2 class="title">What it is — and isn't</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">AgentStateGraph is a <strong style="color:var(--txt)">state primitive</strong>: the layer a next-generation IaC tool, GitOps tool, or agent-native ops platform is built <em>on</em>. That means it is deliberately not a few things.</p>
    <div class="not-grid">
      <div class="notbox"><div class="nt">Not a Terraform replacement</div><div class="nd">Wrong actor model. Terraform assumes humans writing HCL and opening PRs. ASG assumes agents making low-confidence decisions at scale who must be held accountable mechanically.</div></div>
      <div class="notbox"><div class="nt">Not a LangGraph helper</div><div class="nd">Different layer. LangGraph's <code>StateGraph</code> is an in-process dict inside one agent's run. ASG is a persistent, content-addressed substrate used <em>between and above</em> agents.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/compare/">Read the full comparison →</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

